---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { project, socials } from '../data/project';
---
<Base title="Community" description="Find official Scarp accounts, ask language questions, report issues, and connect with the project.">
  <section class="wrap page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The people around the language</p><h1>Bring your curiosity.<br />Find your place.</h1><p class="lead">Ask a question. Share an experiment. Help make the next step clearer.</p></section>
  <section class="wrap community-paths"><a class="news-card" href={`${project.repo}/issues`}><p class="eyebrow">Language & runtime</p><h2>Questions and bugs</h2><p>Use the compiler issue tracker for reproducible problems, language questions, and feature discussions.</p><span class="text-link">Open language issues ↗</span></a><a class="news-card" href="/contribute/"><p class="eyebrow">Make a difference</p><h2>Start contributing</h2><p>Documentation corrections, small examples, and precise bug reports all help move the language forward.</p><span class="text-link">Find a starting point →</span></a></section>
  <section class="wrap section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Official project accounts</p><h2>Follow along.</h2></div><p>Reviewed against the official documentation directory.<br />Some accounts may not have published content yet.</p></div><div class="social-grid">{socials.map(([name, handle, href]) => <a href={href}><span><b>{name}</b><small>{handle}</small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div></section>
  <section class="wrap section prose"><h2>Contact the project</h2><p>For project correspondence: <a href={`mailto:${project.contact}`}>{project.contact}</a>. For a bug, use a public issue so others can inspect the example and follow the resolution.</p><p>The <a href={project.docs + 'community/social'}>official account directory</a> records reviewed channels. Additional invitations and company-page links will appear when their exact destinations are confirmed.</p></section>
</Base>
